From 41deb15612fb5d7befe2e5592ed2a424095a5a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:42:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Map: transparent distance scale, only its bottom line and end
 ticks drawn

The scale's translucent box and its full-height sides covered a strip of
the map. Now there is no ground: just the bottom line, whose length is the
distance, with a short tick up at each end (a flat bracket), in the site's
dark brown with a light casing, and a label with a light halo, so both stay
readable on the warm basemap and on satellite imagery. Clicks and drags
pass through it to the map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc6AVorNUFxs2PasM7foP2
---
Applies with git am on top of the live stack ending in map-scale.patch, lost-towers.patch and
skyline-density.patch (it touches only the scale's two rules in globals.css, so it also applies
straight on map-scale.patch). skylines-page.patch and hide-towers.patch apply cleanly after it.
Revised 12 Oct 2026 16:50 UTC: short ticks up at both ends, on Jeffrey's request.

 src/app/globals.css | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/app/globals.css b/src/app/globals.css
index 68036d8..c556bd4 100644
--- a/src/app/globals.css
+++ b/src/app/globals.css
@@ -47,10 +47,18 @@ body .maplibregl-map { font-family: var(--font); } /* beats maplibre-gl.css, whi
 .app > .map, .app > .map.maplibregl-map { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
 .maplibregl-ctrl-attrib { font-size: 11px; }
 /* Distance scale: bottom right, just above the attribution (the tower panel's bottom edge leaves room for both).
-   Drawn in the site's colours on a translucent ground so it reads on both basemaps ("body" beats maplibre-gl.css,
+   No ground, so it hides as little of the map as it can: only the bottom line, whose length is the distance, with a
+   short tick up at each end (a flat bracket), drawn in the site's dark brown with a light casing (like a road), and a
+   label with a light halo, so both read on the warm basemap and on satellite imagery. Layers, top first: the two
+   ticks and the line, then their casing. Clicks and drags go through to the map ("body" beats maplibre-gl.css,
    which loads later). */
-body .maplibregl-ctrl-bottom-right > .maplibregl-ctrl-scale { margin: 0 10px -4px 0; }
-body .maplibregl-ctrl-scale { background: var(--glass); border-color: var(--fg-2); color: var(--fg); font-size: 11px; line-height: 18px; padding: 0 6px; }
+body .maplibregl-ctrl-bottom-right > .maplibregl-ctrl-scale { margin: 0 10px -2px 0; }
+body .maplibregl-ctrl-scale { --halo: rgba(244,236,233,.9); --ink: linear-gradient(var(--fg), var(--fg)); --cased: linear-gradient(var(--halo), var(--halo));
+  border: 0; color: var(--fg); font-size: 11px; line-height: 14px; padding: 0 5px 4px; pointer-events: none;
+  background: var(--ink) left 1px bottom 1px / 2px 7px, var(--ink) right 1px bottom 1px / 2px 7px, var(--ink) left 1px bottom 1px / calc(100% - 2px) 2px,
+    var(--cased) left bottom / 4px 9px, var(--cased) right bottom / 4px 9px, var(--cased) left bottom / 100% 4px;
+  background-repeat: no-repeat;
+  text-shadow: 1px 0 1px var(--halo), -1px 0 1px var(--halo), 0 1px 1px var(--halo), 0 -1px 1px var(--halo), 0 0 3px var(--halo); }
 .maplibregl-ctrl-group { background: var(--bg-2) !important; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
 .maplibregl-ctrl-bottom-left { z-index: 12; }
 .maplibregl-ctrl-group button + button { border-top-color: var(--line) !important; }
